@startuml neural-rescorer
' rescore_paths: the n-gram beam (blue) hands its candidate paths to the neural rescorer
' (green), which truncates to top_k, scores each path by MLM pseudo-perplexity, squashes
' the perplexity into a bounded score, mixes it with the n-gram score, and re-sorts.
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/neural-rescorer.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/components/neural/rescorer.md §3.
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
skinparam activity {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BackgroundColor #2E7D32
  BorderColor #263238
  DiamondBackgroundColor #ECEFF1
  DiamondFontColor #263238
  DiamondBorderColor #90A4AE
}
title ModernBertRescorer::rescore_paths — two-pass re-ranking of an n-gram beam

|#E3F2FD|n-gram beam (blue)|
start
:**Vec<ScoredPath<W>>**
tokens · ngram_score · final_score = ngram_score;<<#1565C0>>
:sort by final_score, descending;<<#1565C0>>
:**truncate to top_k**   (default 100)
— everything below the cut is discarded, never scored;<<#1565C0>>

|#E8F5E9|ModernBertRescorer (green)|
:chunk the survivors by batch_size (default 32);
repeat :take the next chunk;
  repeat :take the next path in the chunk;
    :text ← tokens.join(" ");
    if (use_pseudo_perplexity?) then (true — default)
      :**PPPL(W) = exp(−PLL(W)/T)**
      one masked forward pass per token
      (see the pseudo-perplexity figure);
    else (false)
      :**embedding coherence**
      2 / (cos(v_W, v_½₁) + cos(v_W, v_½₂) + ε);
    endif
    :**squash:  s_neural = 1 / (1 + score) ∈ (0, 1]**
    lower perplexity ⟹ higher s_neural;
    :**mix:  s_final = α·s_ngram + β·s_neural**
    α = ngram_weight (0.7) · β = neural_weight (0.3);
  repeat while (more paths in chunk?) is (yes)
  ->no;
repeat while (more chunks?) is (yes)
->no;
:re-sort by s_final, descending;

|#E3F2FD|caller|
:**re-ranked Vec<ScoredPath<W>>**
neural_score = Some(s_neural) on every survivor;<<#1565C0>>
stop

note right
  **Scale warning.** s_neural ∈ (0, 1] but s_ngram is
  whatever W converts to through Into<f64>. A raw
  log-probability is negative and unbounded below, so
  α·s_ngram + β·s_neural is then dominated by the n-gram
  term regardless of α, β. Feed the mixer a //bounded//
  n-gram score — e.g. exp(length-normalized log-prob), or
  a min-max normalization over the beam — or reproduce
  the mixture yourself in the log domain.
end note

@enduml
